id: P-warpline-cli-battle-test-periodic-firsthand-dogfood
name: Warpline CLI battle-test (periodic firsthand dogfood)
description: Periodically dogfood the Warpline CLI FIRSTHAND through pseudo-real-life scenarios — the team actually runs the commands on real branches + throwaway swarm repos, captures what works vs what breaks, and files findings. Run this after CLI/engine changes and on a periodic cadence, not just once.
trigger:
  - warpline battle-test
  - battletest warpline
  - dogfood the cli
  - test the warpline cli
  - periodic warpline test
  - battle test the cli
tags:
  - warpline
  - cli
  - dogfood
  - qa
  - battle-test
symbols:
  - '#warpline-cli'
  - '#oracle'
  - '#consolidate'
steps:
  - action: run
    command: cd packages/warpline && npm run build
    notes: 'Build the CLI first so agents test the current code. Invocation: node packages/warpline/dist/cli.js <cmd> from repo root.'
  - action: run
    notes: 'Dispatch the team to run FIRSTHAND in parallel, each a distinct lens: Cid = daily-driver flows (oracle/weave --vs-git/diff/consolidate on DIVERGING branches — merged ones give empty results); Nora (ftux) = cold-newcomer friction (--help, blind commands, first-impression with the raw stderr flood); Jinx = break it (bad/degenerate/injection refs, --json validity, and the SILENT-LIE hunt — confident green on a real conflict is the worst class); Loid = the multi-agent dogfood (build a throwaway swarm repo, consolidate N branches, measure K_human vs git, + Paradigm symbol alignment).'
  - action: verify
    notes: 'Each agent reports the REAL command + observed output + a works/doesn''t verdict + confidence (0-1). Tip: 2>/dev/null to read clean output past the .purpose warning flood. Separate ''crashes/ugly'' from ''lies green''.'
  - action: create
    notes: Synthesize works-vs-doesn't; file each finding as a paradigm task (tag battle-test, mark lies-green findings high); record a review-type lore entry. Re-run periodically as the CLI grows.
